  "definition": "Customer Privacy",
  "effectiveDate": "1999-07-24",
  "historyNote": "#7064, eff 7-24-99",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 3204.08",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 3204.08 Customer Privacy",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3204.08 Customer Privacy.\n\n(a) Consistent with the provisions of RSA 406-C:9 a financial institution shall not use any non-public customer information, other than information pertaining solely to insurance transactions between a customer and the financial institution or its affiliate or subsidiary, or provide such non-public customer information to a third party for the purpose of selling or soliciting the purchase of insurance unless the customer has provided a written consent to use such non-public customer information for insurance solicitation and it is clearly and conspicuously disclosed to the customer that the non-public customer information may be so used.\n\n(b) All completed insurance applications shall be returned only to the licensed insurance agent and under no circumstances shall the financial institution indicate that such applications be returned to an unlicensed financial institution.\n\nSource. #7064, eff 7-24-99",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3200.html"
}
